WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.810
On Dundrum Bay, below
the Mourne Mountains,

2
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:07.650
lies a dune system estimated
at up to 6,000 years old.

3
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:12.270
In 1967, Murlough became
Ireland's first nature reserve.

4
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.930
It holds 21 butterfly species,
among them the marsh fritillary,

5
00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.010
threatened throughout Europe.

6
00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:23.690
Yet here, a thorny shrub is
being dug out: sea buckthorn.

7
00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:27.290
A five-year project aims
to clear about 4 hectares.

8
00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:30.170
Someone planted it to
hold the dunes in place.

9
00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:32.730
So why is it now being dug out?

10
00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:36.070
In this mission, you'll walk
a transect across Murlough,

11
00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:39.290
from moving sand to acidic, leached heath.

12
00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:42.550
Then you'll check each
habitat's official condition.

13
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:47.960
Your mission: explain why a shrub planted
to protect the dunes is now being removed.
